  "description": "Measures hyperbolicity of every branch closure of the atom H_n(q) element at A = 1 (proton, neutron -- never checked before) and A = 2 (deuteron, independently re-running the sibling's 32). This is the one question the sorry-free convexity bound reduces everything to: |tr_M(atom)| <= max_b |J_{K_b}(q)|, so only the largest branch matters. Carries a positive control (figure-eight must read 2.0298832...) and a negative control (trefoil must not read geometric), because 'all non-hyperbolic' is uninterpretable from a detector that can only say zero.",
